<title>UK: Independent forecasts for UK RPIX steady at 2.6%.</title>
<headline>Independent forecasts for UK RPIX steady at 2.6%.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent forecasts for underlying 1996 UK retail price inflation averaged 2.6 percent in September, unchanged from August, according to the latest summary of independent forecasts compiled by the Treasury.</p>
<p>The following are key forecasts from the Treasury</p>
<p>compilation (annual percentage changes unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>    AVERAGE OF NEW FORECASTS		 1996	1997</p>
<p>    GDP					     2.2	 3.3</p>
<p>    RPI (Q4)					2.1	 3.4</p>
<p>    RPIX (Q4)				     2.6	 2.8</p>
<p>    Unemployment (Q4, millions)	     2.07	1.91</p>
<p>    Current account deficit (bln stg)     4.9	 6.8</p>
<p>    PSBR (bln stg)			     27.7	23.1</p>
<p>    Interest rates (Q4)			 5.77	6.95</p>
<p>NOTE: RPI is retail price index. RPIX is retail price index</p>
<p>excluding mortgage interest payments (underlying inflation).</p>
<p>PSBR is public sector borrowing requirement (budget deficit) and</p>
<p>estimates are for the financial year to April 5.</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
